Rockchip RGA: let drivers/video/ enter the rockchip/ vendor directory for
built-in users as well.

drivers/video/Makefile only descends into rockchip/ when
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_SERVICE is set, and that symbol is a tristate that this
target builds as "m".  A directory reached that way is built in module context
only, so obj-y entries inside it (the RGA driver, CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MULTI_RGA=y)
never get linked into vmlinux and /dev/rga is never created.

Add a second descent keyed on CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MULTI_RGA so the directory is
also visited in the built-in pass; the per-entry obj-$(CONFIG_...) rules inside
then keep MPP a module and make RGA part of vmlinux.

--- a/drivers/video/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/video/Makefile
@@ -17,3 +17,4 @@
 # Rockchip vendor video codec (MPP) stack; tristate only, so it is never part
 # of vmlinux - the whole directory builds solely into rk_vcodec.ko.
 obj-$(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_SERVICE) += rockchip/
+obj-$(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MULTI_RGA) += rockchip/
